KEY FINDINGS CARRIED INTO THE RUNBOOK
  - 10 in-scope filings ride this single integration.
  - The AEE is NOT acceptance; the certificat de conformite (code 11) is. A
    structurally invalid file still returns HTTP 200 + AEE.
  - Only unitary deposit (one S20 block) is supported, and violating it fails
    ASYNCHRONOUSLY — after the deadline.
  - The inbound leg is statutorily mandatory: the DGFiP withholding rate reaches
    payroll only as CRM 94. No rate API exists.
  - CRM 34 (AT/MP) must be DERIVED, not posted verbatim, for reduced-rate cases.
  - Returns are purged at 3 months and not archived — the audit trail is a
    Mercans-side obligation.
  - No OAuth2. The API reuses the portal credential triplet with the password sent
    in clear in the body (TLS only). The concentrateur model avoids per-client
    credential custody and is the recommended design.

EFFORT: 59 person-days engineering; 12-16 weeks elapsed, gated by the GIP-MDS
  charte approval (human gate, NO published SLA — flagged as the largest schedule
  risk and explicitly labelled an assumption, not a sourced fact).
